{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall give to the Levites, etc.</b> That is, although HaShem commanded that the Levites have no portion or inheritance in the land, still, by way of kindness they shall give them a free gift from what has come to them — as it is proper to sustain one whose means have not sufficed (perhaps the text should read: whose means have not reached). This is what the verse is precise in saying <b>cities to dwell in</b> — meaning, because of the necessity to dwell in them, etc. And therefore it afterward repeats <b>and the cities shall be to them to dwell in</b> — to alert you that the first statement of ״to dwell in״ is the reason for the giving, while the statement ״and the cities shall be to them to dwell in״ comes to tell you that they must be fit for habitation. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Makkot 12a; Arakhin 33b) that this comes to tell you that the cities must be for habitation, that they do not make a city into a migrash (open land)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The Hebrew contains a parenthetical variant note, apparently by the editor or a scribe, proposing an alternative reading of the phrase שמפרנסים מי שהשיגה ידו. I have translated the variant note exactly as it appears in the parenthetical, preserving both readings."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:17.528690693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}